<div class="common_text"><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;m;margin-bottom: 13pt;line-height: 1.38;"><span style="color: #000000e8;font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;">It's a smart investment—saving on <a href="https://easyhomeservice.com/electrical">electricity</a> costs, increasing the value of a home, and contributing to making the world a greener place. But suppose your system isn't delivering the energy savings you were promised?</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">If you’re a homeowner or small business owner noticing underperformance from your solar setup, you're not alone. There are a few common issues that can affect solar efficiency, and addressing them early can help you get the most out of your investment.</span></p><p></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #04d36f;">1. Shading: The Silent Energy Thief</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><img src="https://easyhomeservice.com/blog/admin/postimages/Shading The Silent Energy Thief.jpg"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif;font-size: 14pt;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Even the partial shadows of nearby trees, chimneys, or buildings can slice the production of your solar panels in half. Because most systems are wired in series which connecting solar panel to the battery, if one panel is shaded, it can drag down the performance of the entire array—just like a kink in a garden hose reducing water flow.</span></p><p></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: black;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><i class="fas fa-lightbulb" style="/* font-size: 15px; */color: #1f2758;"></i> What to do:</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;text-wrap-mode: wrap;color: #000000e8;">Trim overhanging branches or remove small obstructions if possible.&nbsp;</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;text-wrap-mode: wrap;color: #000000e8;">Consider installing microinverters or power optimizers, which are programmable and can run each panel independently, optimizing the performance even under partial shading conditions.</span></p></li></ul><p></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #04d36f;">2. Poor Installation or Design</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><img src="https://easyhomeservice.com/blog/admin/postimages/Poor Installation or Design.jpg"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif;font-size: 14pt;white-space-collapse: preserve;">Performance of solar panels starts with proper planning and installation. In case you have had a poor installation or an installation that was not taking your home solar exposure and energy needs in mind, you may be facing built-in inefficiencies.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Red flags are:</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Panels not true south (in the U.S.)</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Sloping panels at the wrong angles</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Loose wiring or poorly secured mounts</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Inadequate airflow causing overheating</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">What to do</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Schedule a system inspection by a trained solar technician.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Ask for a performance test and pictures of your existing installation to determine installation errors.</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #04d36f;">3. Inverter Failures</span> <img src="https://easyhomeservice.com/blog/admin/postimages/Inverter Failures.jpg"></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif;font-size: 14pt;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Your solar panels generate DC (direct current) electricity, which your home requires AC (alternating current). It is the inverter that does the conversion so that the energy is usable for you to consume or store. When your inverter is not working optimally, the return from your entire system suffers—though your panels themselves might be working fine.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Signs of inverter issues:</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Warning lights or error codes</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">A noticeable drop in solar production on your monitoring app</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Humming or overheating from the inverter box</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">What to do:</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Check the inverter display for errors.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Call your service provider or installer for repair and potential replacement.</span></p></li></ul><p><br><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #04d36f;">4.&nbsp; Outdated or Low-Efficiency Panels</span></p><img src="https://easyhomeservice.com/blog/admin/postimages/Outdated or Low-Efficiency Panels.jpg"><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif;font-size: 14pt;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">If your solar panels were installed more than 10 years ago, they might not meet current performance standards. Even good-quality panels degrade over time, usually losing 0.5 -- 1% per annum. Low-quality panels will degrade faster.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">What to do</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Inspect your original installation instructions for panel performance and manufacturer warranty.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Consider replacing with fresh, high-efficiency panels if your current panels are old or already developing signs of deterioration.</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #04d36f;">5. Lack of Maintenance</span></p><p><img src="https://easyhomeservice.com/blog/admin/postimages/Lack of Maintenance.jpg"><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif;font-size: 14pt;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Dust,&nbsp; pollens, bird droppings, and litter can deposit a thin layer that reduces the absorption of sunlight. Soiling can reduce performance by 10–20% over time.</span><br></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">What to do:</span></p><ul style="margin-bottom: 0px; padding-inline-start: 48px;"><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 15pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Clean panels every 6–12 months, particularly in dusty or high-pollen locations.</span></p></li><li dir="ltr" aria-level="1" style="list-style-type: disc; font-size: 15pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space: pre;"><p dir="ltr" role="presentation" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 15pt; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; text-wrap-mode: wrap;">Inspect wiring and&nbsp; mounts annually for wear or corrosion..</span></p></li></ul><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 24pt; margin-bottom: 3pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 26pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; background-color: transparent; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Here five reason why your solar panel going high&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;background-color: transparent;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Installing <a href="https://easyhomeservice.com/solar">solar panal</a> is a significant step toward energy independence, environmental sustainability, and long-term cost savings. For many U.S. homeowners, going solar is a wise financial investment with the promise of lower utility bills. However, some homeowners are surprised to see their energy bills remain high—or even increase—after making the switch.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">If this sounds familiar, you’re not alone. Several common factors can limit your savings or cause unexpected energy costs after going solar. The good news is that many of these issues can be identified and resolved with simple strategies.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Below are five reasons your energy bills may still be higher than expected—and how to address them effectively.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">1. Increased Energy Consumption After Installation</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Many homeowners naturally assume that once they install solar, they can use electricity with greater freedom. This results in the so-called "solar rebound effect"— a subtle boost of usage due to the feeling that energy is somehow "free". <strong>Working from home</strong>,  increased use of HVAC systems, or operating appliances during peak periods can all lead to increased overall use.</span></p><p><br></p><p><span style="font-family: Georgia, serif; font-size: 14pt; font-weight: 700; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Solution:</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Start&nbsp; by monitoring your electricity consumption by your utility company or a home energy monitor smart device. The devices provide actual-time information for your daily load, allowing you to identify which areas can lower usage. Run heavy-load equipment such as washing machines, dishwashers, and dryers during the daylight hours to enhance the utilization of solar output.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">2. Major Life Changes or New Electric Devices</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Life changes, and so do energy requirements. If you've just added a new family member, bought an electric vehicle (EV), put in a hot tub, or built a home office, any one of these can significantly boost your home electricity load.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">For example charging an EV on a regular basis can add hundreds of kilowatt-hours to your monthly consumption—much more than most residential solar systems are typically sized to manage.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Solution:</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">If you have experienced a lifestyle change, you might want to look at your current energy usage versus your solar system's ability. You can take advantage of increasing your solar array or adding a solar battery to bank extra power for night use or for peak demand hours.</span></p><p><br><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">3. Rising Utility Rates and Time-of-Use Billing</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Going solar doesn't completely eliminate your relationship with the utility company. Most homeowners remain connected to the grid and continue to receive monthly statements. Increasingly, utilities across the U.S. are implementing Time-of-Use (TOU) rate structures, where electricity costs more during peak hours—typically late afternoons and early evenings.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Additionally, utilities often raise their base rates annually or seasonally, which can impact your bill even if your energy usage stays the same.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Solution:</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Check your utility bill to determine if TOU rates are in effect. If they are, move energy-intensive activities (like EV charging, washing clothes, or using the dishwasher) to off-peak hours—generally midday when your solar array is generating at its best. A home battery may also be a great investment to store excess solar energy and use it when rates are highest.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">4. Underperforming or Dirty Solar Panels</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Your solar panels may not be generating as well as they possibly can. Dust, pollen, leaves, bird droppings, or snow settling on them can decrease their efficiency. Gradually, even minor shading from the growth of trees or nearby buildings can affect performance. Moreover, devices such as inverters can deteriorate or fail with no apparent indication.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Solution:</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Regularly monitor your system’s performance using the monitoring platform provided by your installer. If your production is lower than expected, arrange for a professional cleaning and check. Most homeowners find an annual service call helpful to maximize panel performance.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 18pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">5. Energy Inefficiencies within the Home</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;">
  <span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Solar panels by themselves cannot make up for a home that is energy-inefficient.Poor insulation, outdated <a href="https://easyhomeservice.com/hvac"> HVAC systems </a>, drafty <a href="https://easyhomeservice.com/window"> windows, </a>or older appliances can cause energy consumption to rise unnecessarily,offsetting the benefits of solar.</span>
</p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Solution:</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Consider having a professional home energy audit performed. Many local utilities or energy companies offer them for free or at a low cost.The audit will indicate the points of energy loss and suggest specific upgrades including sealing air leaks, improving insulation, installing efficient lighting, and implementing smart thermostats.These small modifications can translate to big long-term savings.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Stay Proactive to Maximize Solar Savings</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Going solar is a great and environmentally conscious decision—but it's not a "set it and forget it" proposition.To maximize the rewards of your investment, it's necessary to keep an eye on usage, keep your system in good repair, and keep your home as efficient as possible.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">By taking these five proactive steps, U.S. homeowners can keep utility bills low, enhance their solar system value, and further minimize grid dependency.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Here You Can Understand How Much Your Solar Panel Will Cost</span><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br><br></span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Initial Investment vs. Long-Term Savings</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Solar panels are a smart investment for homeowners looking to reduce energy bills and increase property value. But like any major home upgrade, solar energy systems require some level of upkeep. While maintenance is generally low, understanding the associated costs and how to manage them can help you protect your investment and ensure long-term savings</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Initial Investment vs. Long-Term Savings</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;break-after: avoid;color: #000000e8;">While the initial cost of installing a solar panel system is between $10,000 and $30,000, depending on the size and complexity of the system, federal and state incentives or financing are offered to many homeowners that reduce the initial expenses.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">The good news? After they are installed, solar panels and accessories will generally last for 25 to 30 years and can significantly reduce or eliminate altogether—monthly power bills. Ultimately, savings accrue to much more than the cost. Maintenance does come into play in ensuring this return on investment, though.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Typical Annual Maintenance Tasks</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Solar panels are supposed to be low maintenance, but they're not entirely hands-off. What are some common routine maintenance items homeowners need to know</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Cleaning Panels</span><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">:</span><span style="font-size: 12pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> </span><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;">Dust, leaves, and bird droppings can cut efficiency. Soft cleaning 1–2 times a year should be enough.</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Checking for Damage:</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> Harsh weather or rubbish can lead to cracks or wear. Regular checking once a year prevents problems arising early.</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Testing Inverter Performance: </span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">The inverter, that transforms solar power into useful electricity, can need servicing or replacement every 10–15 years.</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Monitoring Output:</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> Most modern systems come with digital apps to track energy output. Unusual dips might indicate maintenance requirements.</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"><br></span></p>
<p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Factors That Affect Maintenance Costs</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-weight: 700;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">Solar panel maintenance cost depends on various factors:</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"></span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">System Size:</span><span style="font-size: 16pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;">Bigger systems can take longer and more effort to clean and inspect.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Location &amp; Climate:</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> Locations with high pollen, dust, or snow levels might need cleaning more often.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Type of Mounting:</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;"> Roof-mounted systems are harder (and sometimes more expensive) to access than ground-mounted ones.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Panel Quality</span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">: Higher-quality panels tend to need less maintenance and have longer warranties.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt;margin-bottom: 0pt;line-height: 1.38;color: #000000e8;"><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Age of the System: </span><span style="font-size: 16pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-variant-position: normal; font-variant-emoji: normal; vertical-align: baseline; white-space-collapse: preserve;">Older systems may require more frequent inspections or component replacement.</span></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 14pt;font-family: Georgia, serif;font-variant-numeric: normal;font-variant-east-asian: normal;font-variant-alternates: normal;font-variant-position: normal;font-variant-emoji: normal;vertical-align: baseline;white-space-collapse: preserve;color: #000000e8;">On average, homeowners can expect to pay between $150 to $300 per year for basic cleaning and inspection services. Repairs or inverter replacements can add several hundred dollars more depending on the issue.</span></p><p><br></p><p dir="ltr" style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; line-height: 1.38;"><span style="font-size: 20pt; font-family: Georgia, serif; font-weight: 700; font-variant-numeric: normal; font-variant-east-asian: normal; font-variant-alternates: normal; font-